Work around nvcc naming inline_scheduler's private sender in a static_assert.

nvcc 12.9 expands schedule_result_t<inline_scheduler> to the private __sender
type in its generated host code, which GCC 12 then rejects. Check the sender's
environment type directly under nvcc; get_env() returns __inline_attrs. Other
compilers retain the assertion through schedule_result_t.

Keep this separate from the original nvcc patch so an existing FetchContent
checkout with those workarounds already applied can acquire this fix too.

